Workstream ID: atlas-progression-redesign
Title: Research-led Atlas expeditions and meaningful work progression
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make real checkpoint work lead to clear, inviting fictional rewards
Dependencies: discovery-atlas, tracker-foundation, tutorial-and-help
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/24
Purpose: Research progression across several games and motivation studies,
  document transferable mechanisms and their limits, and implement a stronger
  optional Discovery Atlas loop. Improve the invitation to do real work, not
  time spent clicking, fabricated ability or compulsive engagement.

Tasks:
  [x] Review multiple source-backed game case studies and motivation evidence.
  [x] Document findings, tradeoffs, rejected mechanics and the chosen design.
  [x] Connect real saved work to readable near-term progress and reward previews.
  [x] Offer useful checkpoint expeditions without changing mission authority.
  [x] Preserve the Discovered default and existing collection/provenance.
  [x] Preserve records, criteria, verified lineage, backups and tutorial isolation.
  [x] Qualify affected domain, native-browser, motion and rendering boundaries.
  [x] Update affected guides, source rationale and local continuity.
  [x] Synchronize this workstream and verify its original issue/Project identity.

Acceptance criteria:
  Research distinguishes developer statements, documented mechanics, inference,
    experimental results and unverified effects in this learning workspace.
  Useful saved work can visibly advance the journey without requiring a new
    entry in the finite 24-discovery collection.
  The next real action and its deterministic reward are understandable; preview,
    browsing, replay and timers never create progress or complete a checkpoint.
  Completion remains an explicit evidence/criteria confirmation, and planned,
    blocked, completed and archived mission boundaries remain authoritative.
  Repeated records cannot farm the same checkpoint award, verified append
    lineage deduplicates, and future local calendar days remain excluded.
  No random loot, purchase, streak punishment, FOMO, leaderboard, new telemetry,
    automatic publication or functional learning-tool gate is introduced.
  Existing saved formats and ordinary/encrypted backup behavior are compatible.
  Original 3D work remains bounded, event-driven and accessible without WebGL;
    deliberate previews must be labelled unearned and cannot change ownership.
  Both themes, narrow layouts, keyboard, reduced motion and tutorial coexistence
    receive focused qualification using only disposable fictional records.
  Technical completion is separate from human aesthetic/motivational acceptance.
  This workstream is local research/implementation, not a new source push,
    deployment, workflow change or publication authorization.

